WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.230
Now, when building out designs in

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.510
front-end interfaces, one of the tools

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.030
that you do need to be familiar with is

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.790
this newer tool by Anthropic called

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.510
Claude Design. So, you can see right

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.950
now, as of the time of this recording,

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.110
it's still on beta, but I do advise you

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.550
to try it out because as they're

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.510
building up this software, it is very

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:17.870
clear that at some point they're going

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.350
to merge Claude Code and Claude Design

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.990
so that the integrations here are much

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.790
more seamless. And so, in this set of

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.670
lessons, what you'll understand is how

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.070
to use Claude Design and how to

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.350
integrate it with Claude Code so that if

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.390
you need visual interface when dealing

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.510
with front-end design, you can actually

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.870
use this tool in order to turbocharge

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.720
your workflows.
